# FL4's trusted base (DESIGN.md §9): what the proofs assume rather than
# prove. `cargo xtask trusted` checks that every path exists and reports the
# size of each entry; CI prints the report, so growth shows in review.
#
# Lines are `<group>: <path>`; a directory counts all its source files.
# Tools (Rust, LLVM, the linker, Charon, Aeneas, Lean) and the processor's
# memory model are trusted too but are not in this repository.

# Boot and entry: assembly and the glue around it.
entry: crates/fl4-kernel/src
entry: crates/fl4-kernel-aarch64/src
entry: crates/fl4-efi/src
entry: crates/fl4-bootinfo/src

# Hardware backends.
hardware: crates/fl4-arch-x86_64/src
hardware: crates/fl4-arch-aarch64/src

# fl4-core's AArch64 slice: compiled only with `--features aarch64`, so
# not extracted by Charon/Aeneas (`cargo xtask extract` builds the x86_64
# core) and not covered by the proofs.
unverified-core: crates/fl4-core/src/arch/aarch64

# The kernel entry runtime: the serial gate, the local paths beside it and
# their object locks (tested by fl4-sim, DESIGN.md §7, §10).
runtime: crates/fl4-store/src
runtime: crates/fl4-sync/src

# The interface between the verified core and the trusted world: what P0
# assumes the Store and Arch implementations do.
interface: crates/fl4-core/src/machine.rs
interface: proofs/Fl4Proofs/P0/Totality.lean
interface: proofs/Fl4Core/FunsExternal.lean

# The abstract model of the transactional runtime P2 was proved about,
# superseded with it (DESIGN.md §9).
model: proofs/Fl4Proofs/P2/Runtime.lean
